### Variáveis (edite se mudou alguma porta)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@mockUrl = http://localhost:8082

### ============================================================
### Health checks
### ============================================================

### API - liveness (porta de management 8081, não a 8080)
GET http://localhost:8081/actuator/health/liveness HTTP/1.1

### API - readiness na porta de management 8081 (exige PostgreSQL)
GET http://localhost:8081/actuator/health/readiness HTTP/1.1

### Worker - liveness (porta de management 8083)
GET http://localhost:8083/actuator/health/liveness HTTP/1.1

### Worker - readiness (exige PostgreSQL + Kafka)
GET http://localhost:8083/actuator/health/readiness HTTP/1.1

### Partner mock - health
GET {{mockUrl}}/actuator/health HTTP/1.1

### ============================================================
### POST /pix - criar transação (id único a cada envio)
### Resposta esperada: 202 Accepted
### ============================================================

POST {{baseUrl}}/pix HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "tx-{{$guid}}",
  "amount": 150.75,
  "pixKey": "cliente@email.com",
  "description": "Pagamento de fatura"
}

### ============================================================
### Fluxo manual: cria e consulta a mesma transação
### Edite o @txId abaixo e execute 1 e 2 em ordem
### ============================================================

@txId = tx-demo-001

### 1. Criar
POST {{baseUrl}}/pix HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "{{txId}}",
  "amount": 42.50,
  "pixKey": "demo@email.com",
  "description": "Teste manual"
}

### 2. Consultar (usa o mesmo @txId acima)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pix/{{txId}} HTTP/1.1

### ============================================================
### Idempotência - mesmo transactionId, mesmo payload
### 1ª chamada: 202 | 2ª chamada: 202 (PROCESSING) ou 200 (SUCCESS/FAILED)
### Nada novo é criado
### ============================================================

### 1. Primeira chamada -> 202
POST {{baseUrl}}/pix HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "tx-idempotente-001",
  "amount": 100.00,
  "pixKey": "cliente@email.com",
  "description": "Pagamento de fatura"
}

### 2. Repetição idêntica -> 202 ou 200, sem duplicar
POST {{baseUrl}}/pix HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "tx-idempotente-001",
  "amount": 100.00,
  "pixKey": "cliente@email.com",
  "description": "Pagamento de fatura"
}

### ============================================================
### Conflito - mesmo transactionId, payload diferente -> 409
### ============================================================

POST {{baseUrl}}/pix HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "tx-idempotente-001",
  "amount": 999.99,
  "pixKey": "outro@email.com",
  "description": "Outro pagamento"
}

### ============================================================
### Validação - payload inválido -> 400
### ============================================================

POST {{baseUrl}}/pix HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "",
  "amount": -5,
  "pixKey": "",
  "description": "Payload inválido"
}

### ============================================================
### GET - transação inexistente -> 404
### ============================================================

GET {{baseUrl}}/pix/tx-que-nao-existe HTTP/1.1

### ============================================================
### Partner mock - trocar cenário (útil p/ testar retry/DLQ)
### success | flaky | always-500 | always-400 | slow
### ============================================================

### Ver estatísticas do mock
GET {{mockUrl}}/partner/admin/stats HTTP/1.1

### Forçar falhas transitórias (2x 503 e depois 200)
POST {{mockUrl}}/partner/admin/scenario HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mode": "FLAKY",
  "latencyMs": 200,
  "failTimes": 2,
  "slowDelayMs": 6000
}

### Forçar erro permanente (sempre 400 -> FAILED, sem retry)
POST {{mockUrl}}/partner/admin/scenario HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mode": "ALWAYS_400",
  "latencyMs": 100,
  "failTimes": 2,
  "slowDelayMs": 6000
}

### Voltar ao sucesso
POST {{mockUrl}}/partner/admin/scenario HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mode": "SUCCESS",
  "latencyMs": 200,
  "failTimes": 2,
  "slowDelayMs": 6000
}

### Resetar estatísticas do mock
POST {{mockUrl}}/partner/admin/reset HTTP/1.1
